md(4): read hint.md.N.len with resource_long_value() into a size_t, so a
ram disk of 4 GiB or more attaches whole instead of truncated to len mod
2^32, or skipped when the size is a multiple of 4 GiB.

Tutorial: FreeBSD/docs/md_preload_len.md
Reported by: llm-postcr, POSTCR-46c2d93c572865f6441788ad8416ff7ff971829a-2
Base: main at 75734a4b6d0b (2026-11-08).

diff --git a/sys/dev/md/md.c b/sys/dev/md/md.c
index f29490d12b85..0875832d667b 100644
--- a/sys/dev/md/md.c
+++ b/sys/dev/md/md.c
@@ -2080,7 +2080,7 @@ g_md_init(struct g_class *mp __unused)
 	caddr_t mod;
 	u_char *ptr, *name, *type;
 	u_char scratch[40];
-	unsigned len;
+	size_t len;
 	int i;
 	vm_offset_t paddr;
 
@@ -2129,7 +2129,7 @@ g_md_init(struct g_class *mp __unused)
 	for (int i = 0; i < 32; i++) {
 		if (resource_long_value("md", i, "physaddr",
 			(long *) &paddr) != 0 ||
-		    resource_int_value("md", i, "len", &len) != 0)
+		    resource_long_value("md", i, "len", (long *)&len) != 0)
 		        break;
 		/*
 		 * Map the memory into the kernel pmap, if not already present.
